            <ArticleTitle>Saphenous vein graft aneurysm presenting as a large mediastinal mass compressing the right atrium.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>706-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with a large saphenous vein graft aneurysm is described. This case illustrates the role of magnetic resonance imaging and cardiac catheterization in patients with a mediastinal mass and history of coronary bypass surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
